I totally commiserate. I think I had one Valk I got all the way into
the Maze levels... having found only two scrolls of identify (both
blessed, both still only identified a single inventory item) the
entire way. No magic markers, no +of Identify, no touchstones, no
helpful thrones, nothing. The equipment I had that I knew what it was
was great, but there was a bunch of stuff I wasn't sure why I was
toting it all around. (Can't remember why she died or if it had to do
with item ignorance) On the plus side she at least got pretty far, but
it was still frustrating not knowing what all my item options were.

Even with other ways of "identifying" items there are points where you
just need to know exactly what something is (or especially in the case
of wands, how many charges it has. Don't want that Wand of Teleport or
digging you're counting on to save your life run out of charges before
you expect it to). Price-ID only goes so far too... sure it's easy to
Price-ID Identify or Enchant Armor, but what about scrolls of genocide
and punishment? Don't want to confuse one for the other (those may not
be the same price but I know there are a few same-price scrolls in the
higher price area, some of which are real bad and some real good--and
when you're getting deeper into the dungeon, you need to know which is
which).

It's frustrating but just one of those weird RNG things... since
identify usually drops frequently enough. (Although I'm still of the
opinion blessed scrolls should always ID everything in your pack just
in case that's the only one you ever find, but got forbid anything
makes playing Nethack easier. ;) )

